Fixed. The two failures were stale test expectations pinning the old buggy behavior the task explicitly said to update — the implementation itself was correct.

What I changed (both in src/git.rs tests):

1. `test_git_subcommand_help — parse_git_args("unknown") and parse_git_args("push") now expect GitSubcommand::Unknown("...") instead of Help`, matching the new honest-error-with-did-you-mean behavior.
2. test_git_subcommand_stash_show — `parse_git_args("stash show abc") now expects BadStashIndex { action: "show", arg: "abc" } instead of the old silent fallback to StashShow(None)` (stash@{0}).

One hiccup worth noting: I initially issued both edits in parallel and the first one got clobbered by the second (same-file race), so I reapplied it — a reminder to serialize edits to the same file.

